# What a land could produce is asked of a permanent whose ability adds X mana in any combination of colors, under a
# mana replacement with no declared contract (CR 106.7, 614.1a). March of the Machines makes Bot2's Wizard's Rockets
# an artifact creature, then Bot2's Arcane Adaptation naming Saproling makes it a Saproling and Life and Limb a Forest
# land, each later than the one before (CR 613.7: timestamp order); Bot2's Llanowar Elves becomes a Forest too. Bot2 activates Deep Water ("until end of turn, if
# you tap a land you control for mana, it produces {U} instead of any other type"), and Bot1's Exotic Orchard asks
# at Bot1's next priority what Bot2's lands could produce. The query once hit an `assert` there and crashed the game.
# Under Deep Water Bot2's Islands and the Rockets could produce only {U}: the Orchard names blue and nothing else. The
# turn after, Deep Water's effect has ended and the Rockets' any color is back.
